speechtext:
This sum is
for the usual drainage and road making,
I suppose? There are some reserves in the province of Quebec in which it is a constant complaint that the roads passing through the reserve are not kept in repair. In the Caughnawaga reserve, for instance, the roads are in a very bad condition and are a serious impediment to traffic. I do not know whether that matter has been called to the attention of my hon. friend.
